//! GitHub-style `:shortcode:` emoji. Changelogs written for GitHub (release
//! notes generated by gitmoji-style tools in particular) arrive on
//! CurseForge and Modrinth with their shortcodes still as text, like
//! `:sparkles: New Features`. These turn into the emoji GitHub would show.
//! Only known codes change; anything else (a time like `10:30:45`, a code we
//! don't know) stays as written.

